{"id":"1405ec09-982c-4f91-8eeb-2f83e5470ea5","object":"chat.completion","created":1784823061,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    state = payload['initial_state']\\n    max_steps = payload['max_steps']\\n    transitions = payload['transitions']\\n    tool_obs = payload['tool_observations']\\n    for _ in range(max_steps):\\n        tr = transitions[state]\\n        if tr['kind'] == 'final':\\n            return tr['value']\\n        action = tr['action']\\n        obs = tool_obs[action]\\n        state = tr['next_by_observation'].get(obs, tr['default_next'])\\n    return None\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" whose value is Python source code defining solve(case). The function must return a JSON-serializable object, not mutate case, use only standard library. The task is from fixture payload: a state machine with transitions, initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations. The function should simulate the agent? Actually the description says \"Registered procedure task AGENT-RA-02\". Likely the agent follows a deterministic policy: given initial state, it performs actions, using tool_observations as the observation from each tool. The transitions are deterministic based on observation. We need to simulate up to max_steps steps, returning the final value or something? The case payload includes initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations (mapping from action to observation), and transitions (state -> {kind, action?, next_by_observation?, default_next?, value?}).\n\nInterpretation: The agent starts at initial_state. At each step, if state is final (kind \"final\"), return its value. Else (kind \"action\"), perform the action (action string). Then look up the observation for that action from tool_observations. Then transition to next state: if observation key exists in next_by_observation, go